{"name":"Dulce de Leche","hex":"#d6851f","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"dulce de leche","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A South American sweet spread made from sugar and boiled milk."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dulce_de_leche"}],"entries":[{"title":"Dulce de leche","blocks":[{"text":"Dulce de leche, caramelized milk, milk candy, or milk jam is a confection commonly made by heating sugar and milk over several hours. The substance takes on a spreadable, sauce-like consistency and derives its rich flavour and colour from non-enzymatic browning. It is typically used to top or fill other sweet foods."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5a/DulceDeLeche.jpg/330px-DulceDeLeche.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dulce_de_leche"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/25/Making_Dulce_de_leche.jpg/500px-Making_Dulce_de_leche.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/25/Making_Dulce_de_leche.jpg/500px-Making_Dulce_de_leche.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMaking_Dulce_de_leche.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c2/Consistency_of_Dulce_de_Leche.jpg/500px-Consistency_of_Dulce_de_Leche.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c2/Consistency_of_Dulce_de_Leche.jpg/1280px-Consistency_of_Dulce_de_Leche.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c2/Consistency_of_Dulce_de_Leche.jpg/500px-Consistency_of_Dulce_de_Leche.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_conte